{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":127,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-2-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","line":377,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[pointwise uniqueness of geodesics]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch3-2-1, lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:2.5}\n  If two curves $\\gamma_1,\\gamma_2$ are base projections of integral curves of the\n  geodesic spray whose lifts agree at $t_0$ (equal initial point \\emph{and} initial\n  velocity), then $\\gamma_1$ and $\\gamma_2$ agree on a neighbourhood of $t_0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  The lifts are integral curves of the same $C^\\infty$ vector field $G$ on $TM$\n  with the same value at $t_0$, so by uniqueness of integral curves\n  (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise}, Gr\\\"onwall) they agree near $t_0$; projecting to $M$\n  gives $\\gamma_1=\\gamma_2$ near $t_0$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[pointwise uniqueness of geodesics] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d322d352d756e69717565\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23def%3Adc-ch3-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch3-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-2-pointwise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:2.5</span></span>If two curves <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma _1,\\gamma _2$\">$\\gamma _1,\\gamma _2$</span> are base projections of integral curves of the geodesic spray whose lifts agree at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_0$\">$t_0$</span> (equal initial point <em>and</em> initial velocity), then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma _1$\">$\\gamma _1$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma _2$\">$\\gamma _2$</span> agree on a neighbourhood of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_0$\">$t_0$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p>The lifts are integral curves of the same <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$C^\\infty $\">$C^\\infty $</span> vector field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$G$\">$G$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$TM$\">$TM$</span> with the same value at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_0$\">$t_0$</span>, so by uniqueness of integral curves (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-2-pointwise\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d322d322d706f696e7477697365\">subsection 1.1</a>, Grönwall) they agree near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_0$\">$t_0$</span>; projecting to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma _1=\\gamma _2$\">$\\gamma _1=\\gamma _2$</span> near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_0$\">$t_0$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-velocity","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch3-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch3-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-velocity","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-velocity","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-velocity"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-5","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-5","label":"prop:dc-ch3-2-5"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-7","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-7","label":"prop:dc-ch3-2-7"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-expmap","title":"def:dc-ch3-expmap","label":"def:dc-ch3-expmap"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[pointwise uniqueness of geodesics]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch3-2-1, lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:2.5}\n  If two curves $\\gamma_1,\\gamma_2$ are base projections of integral curves of the\n  geodesic spray whose lifts agree at $t_0$ (equal initial point \\emph{and} initial\n  velocity), then $\\gamma_1$ and $\\gamma_2$ agree on a neighbourhood of $t_0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  The lifts are integral curves of the same $C^\\infty$ vector field $G$ on $TM$\n  with the same value at $t_0$, so by uniqueness of integral curves\n  (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise}, Gr\\\"onwall) they agree near $t_0$; projecting to $M$\n  gives $\\gamma_1=\\gamma_2$ near $t_0$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch3-2-1","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-2-pointwise","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}